 A case study on the state of civil rights in contemporary Sweden:

HONOURARY DOCTORATE IN RETURN FOR SUPPRESSION OF HUMAN RIGHTS

Last year the university of Lund in Sweden conferred an honourary doctor's 
degree on the President of the European Commission of Human Rights, Prof. Carl 
Aage Noergaard of Denmark. Why ?

On 29 October 1991, the Plenary of the European Court of Human Rights had 
condemned Sweden for holding a secret trial on opinions. A secret trial is  
something which is abhorred by lawyers, democrats and human rights activists the 
world over. The secret trial had been based on groundless accusations, which had 
been levelled by the top administration of the very same university of Lund at 
one of their lecturers, Reinhard Helmers.

In front of the Strasbourg Court, the Swedish Government saw no wrong in openly 
